The view came after the U.S. government made an announcement of artificial intelligence even though the United States itself as a whole lacked official artificial intelligence strategies.
Meanwhile, China introduced its plan last year by aiming to become number 1 in artificial intelligence innovation by 2030.
“Doubpling the allocation of artificial intelligence studies is a good start as all other countries are far behind the United States and we want to gain further success in artificial intelligence,” said Lee
