“China’s National Natural Science Foundation provides funds to people in academic institutions. It’s similar to how the National Science Foundation and other governmental organizations divide the funds into U.S. researchers but the quality of academic work in China is lower,” said Lee.
Earlier this year, the U.S.’s Department of Defense established a Joint Artificial Intelligation Center which aims to gather partners from industries and academies. The White House announced a line-up of Selected Committee for Artificial Intelligence.
