Now in the seventh year, the World People's Festival will see tens of thousands of people gathered at the Central Park Great Site to not just watch performances such as Janet Jackson, Cardi B and Shawn Mendes, but also to raise awareness about the real goal of the event ending extreme poverty by 2030.
The World People's Festival, initiated in 2012, is an extension of the World Poverty Project, an international support group that aims to eradicate poverty by increasing the number of people actively against it.
In order to receive free tickets for this event (unless you're willing to pay VIP tickets), visitors of these concerts will have to complete several tasks, or "actuations" such as becoming a volunteer, sending an e-mail to a world leader, making a phone call or any other meaningful way to help raise awareness about their goal of eradicating poverty.
