The creators of the world's website are planning to start a new internet network to rival Google and Facebook
World Website creator Tim Berners-Lee launched start-up companies to rival Facebook, Amazon and Google.
Inrupt is an open-source company based on Berners-Lee's Solid software.
Solid allows users to choose where their data will be stored and who will be entitled to access the information.
In an exclusive interview with the Fast Company, Berners-Lee joke that Inrupt’s real purpose is “to dominate the world.” ““
“We have to do this now,” he said of this start-up company.”
“It��’s a historic moment.”
The app uses Solid technology that allows people to create their own “personal online data storage” or POD.
It can contain contact lists, daily worklists, calendars, songlists and other personal professional equipment.
It's like Google Drive, Microsoft Outlook, Slack, and Spotify that's available in one browser and simultaneously.
What's unique about the storage of data in this personal tall is that it's up to the user for who can access the required type of information.
The company calls it “personal authority through data.”
Ihlam for Inrupt, according to its CEO John Bruce, is to bring certain resources, processes and expertise to help people enjoy Solid.
The company now consists of Berners-Lee, Bruce, a security platform purchased by IMB, a number of contracted developer staff to work in this project and a voluntary code writer community.
Starting this week, tech developers from all over the world can create their own independent applications without being centered in any location by using the equipment available on the Inrupt website.
Berners-Lee also said he and his team did not have any discussions with “Facebook and Google to unvelocate or not introducing a change where all their business models will change immediately.”
“We aren’t asking their permission.”
In a publication in Medium on Saturday, Bernes-Lee wrote, Inrupt, “the mission is to provide a business energy and an ecosystem to help protect the integrity and quality of new websites built using Solid.” “
In 1994, Berners-Lee changed the world of the Internet when he founded the World Website Consortium at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
In recent months, Berners-Lee has been outspokenly debating about the need for an independent website.
While launching Inrupt, Berners-Lee will remain the Founder and Director of the World Website Consortium, the Web Foundation and the Open Data Institute.
